From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:27:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/40] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: give each
 TFA9873 its own channel and name prefix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both amplifiers sit on the same primary MI2S line. The tfa987x driver picks the TDM slot it
plays from the "sound-channel" property (TFA987X_TDM_CFG6 SPKS) and defaults to 0, so without it
both amplifiers played the left channel. They also registered identical DAPM widgets ("PWUP",
"Speaker"), which ASoC reports as overwritten, so the second amplifier was not reliably powered
and the bottom speaker stayed silent.

Put the earpiece amplifier (0x34) on channel 0 and the loudspeaker (0x35) on channel 1, each
with its own sound-name-prefix.

Signed-off-by: Eduardo García-Mádico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
index a58cc342c..2e9c99f2b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -1065,6 +1065,9 @@ tfa9873_l: codec@34 { /* EAR */
 		reg = <0x34>;
 		reset-gpio = <&tlmm 101 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
+		sound-channel = <0>;
+		sound-name-prefix = "Earpiece";
+
 		#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
 	};
 
@@ -1074,6 +1077,9 @@ tfa9873_r: codec@35 { /* SPK */
 		reg = <0x35>;
 		reset-gpio = <&tlmm 101 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
+		sound-channel = <1>;
+		sound-name-prefix = "Speaker";
+
 		#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
 	};
 };
